man on the sabbath day receive circumcision, that the law of Moses should not be broken; are ye angry at me, because I have made a man every whit whole on the sabbath day?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDJudge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLThen said some of them of Jerusalem, Is not this he, whom they seek to kill?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsBut, lo, he speaketh boldly, and they say nothing unto him. Do the rulers know indeed that this is the very Christ?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Howbeit we know this man whence he is: but when Christ cometh, no man knoweth whence he is.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªThen cried Jesus in the temple as he taught, saying, Ye both know me, and ye know whence I am: and I am not come of myself, but he that sent me is true, whom ye know not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ7But I know him: for I am from him, and he hath sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Then they sought to take him: but no man laid hands on him, because his hour was not yet come.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd many of the people believed on him, and said, When Christ cometh, will he do more miracles than these which this man hath done?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse$¦verses•„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹The Pharisees heard that the people murmured such things concerning him; and the Pharisees and the chief priests sent officers to take him.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaThen said Jesus unto them, Yet a little while am I with you, and then I go unto him that sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPYe shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, thither ye cannot come.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen said the Jews among themselves, Whither will he go, that we shall not find him? will he go unto the dispersed among the Gentiles, and teach the Gentiles?¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|What manner of saying is this that he said, Ye shall seek me, and shall not find me: and where I am, thither ye cannot come?¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book*§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse'¦verses“„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€In the last day, that great day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhHe that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡(But this spake he of the Spirit, which they that believe on him should receive: for the Holy Ghost was not yet given; because that Jesus was not yet glorified.)¦layout ªlast_verse'…¤book*§chapter«first_verse(ªlast_verse,¦verses•„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Many of the people therefore, when they heard this saying, said, Of a truth this is the Prophet.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQOthers said, This is the Christ. But some said, Shall Christ come out of Galilee?¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxHath not the scripture said, That Christ cometh of the seed of David, and out of the town of Bethlehem, where David was?¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8So there was a division among the people because of him.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd some of them would have taken him; but no man laid hands on him.¦layout ªlast_verse,…¤book*§chapter«first_verse-ªlast_verse1¦verses•„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpThen came the officers to the chief priests and Pharisees; and they said unto them, Why have ye not brought him?¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5The officers answered, Never man spake like this man.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ7Then answered them the Pharisees, Are ye also deceived?¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;Have any of the rulers or of the Pharisees believed on him?¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3But this people who knoweth not the law are cursed.¦layout ªlast_verse1…¤book*§chapter«first_verse2ªlast_verse5¦verses”„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙONicodemus saith unto them, (he that came to Jesus by night, being one of them,)¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGDoth our law judge any man, before it hear him, and know what he doeth?¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsThey answered and said unto him, Art thou also of Galilee? Search, and look: for out of Galilee ariseth no prophet.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And every man went unto his own house.¦layout ªlast_verse5